<title>USA: KeyCorp, OfficeMax launch pilot.</title>
<headline>KeyCorp, OfficeMax launch pilot.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>KeyCorp said Thursday it and OfficeMax have agreed to jointly launch a financial services, copying and desktop publishing center in a suburb of Cleveland.</p>
<p>KeyCorp said the center will open during the fourth quarter of this year, and it will be a combination of KeyCorp's KeyCenter, which offers PC-based computers and 24-hour telebanking services, with OfficeMax's CopyMax, which offers digital printing, oversized copying and desktop publishing.</p>
<p>The companies said they hope the center will target serving small business owners.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
